          "start": 0
        },
        "quote": "(a) Credits for Existing Trees. In order to encourage the preservation of existing trees, credits up to 50 percent of required base points may be given in the event existing trees are preserved.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.235.070:block:0#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.235.070 block 1",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 1,
          "component_id": "2da904bc-eb69-550f-9660-a845501e94dc",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 843,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.235.070:block:1",
          "start": 195
        },
        "quote": "For each existing significant tree with a diameter caliper between six inches and 12 inches that is preserved on the landscape plan, a credit of 15 base points will be applied. For each existing significant tree with a D.B.H. between 12 inches and 24 inches, a credit of 20 base points will be applied. For each existing significant tree with a D.B.H. over 24 inches, a credit of 25 base points will be applied. Any significant tree that dies during construction, or because of construction, must be replaced with a tree or trees of a similar species, or a species approved by the City Forester, to equal or exceed the point value of the lost tree.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.235.070:block:1#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.235.070 block 2",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 2,
          "component_id": "5303d76a-80b5-5d86-99af-79cc6206d4b9",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1674,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.235.070:block:2",
          "start": 844
        },
        "quote": "(b) Additional Points Required for Removal of Existing Significant Trees. Any existing significant trees removed from the site shall require additional base points above those calculated for the square footage of the developed area. For trees removed between six inches and 12 inches diameter caliper, an additional 15 base points shall be required. For trees removed between 12 inches and 24 inches D.B.H., an additional 20 base points shall be required. For any trees removed that are larger than 25 inches D.B.H., an additional 25 base points shall be required. If the Planning Director, in consultation with the City Forester, determines that removal of any aforementioned significant trees will not be detrimental to the overall appearance of the development, some or all of these additional point requirements may be waived.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.235.070:block:2#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.235.070 block 3",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 3,
          "component_id": "d6967577-4883-5361-9f8a-e1412e69cf3e",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1890,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.235.070:block:3",
          "start": 1675
        },
        "quote": "(c) Trees for which a developer wishes to receive credit must be within the developed area, and incorporated into an overall landscape design. (Ord. 18255 § 5, 6-1-04; Ord. 17846 § 7, 6-11-02. Code 1995 § 48-38.06.)",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.235.070:block:3#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
